s the nonzero integer 2.","basis_verdict":"applicable","checked_step_ids":["step-substitute"],"claim_id":"b-square-even","reasoning":"The algebra validly gives b^2=2c^2 conditional on square-equation.","verdict":"conditional"},{"basis_reasoning":"step-b-even applies the same divisor-2 parity argument to b^2=2c^2.","basis_verdict":"applicable","checked_step_ids":["step-b-even"],"claim_id":"b-even","reasoning":"The conclusion follows conditional on b-square-even.","verdict":"conditional"},{"basis_reasoning":"step-contradiction uses the discharged local assumption and the proved common-divisor contradiction, but its chain depends on unsupported square-equation.","basis_verdict":"unsupported","checked_step_ids":["step-contradiction"],"claim_id":"sqrt2-irrational","reasoning":"The reductio is logically valid conditional on the missing square-root property; as written, the self-contained derivation is incomplete.","verdict":"conditional"}],"missing_evidence":["A stated definition or derivation that (sqrt(2))^2=2 is needed for step-square and hence for the unconditional irrationality conclusion."],"recommended_action":"revise","tool_requests":[]}
